---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import MazeField from "../components/MazeField.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Maze Field — Ryan Sheridan"
  description="A generated maze background with a ball the cursor drags through it."
  noindex
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="maze-page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>Maze field</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        A perfect maze carved by randomized depth-first search, drawn behind the
        content. The ball routes to the room the cursor is in the way the maze
        allows, threading the gaps between rows and columns and never crossing a
        wall. Park the cursor on the far side of a wall and it takes the long
        way round to reach you.
      </p>
      <p class="intro note">
        The 404 page runs this pattern for real. Contact still uses the compass
        cursor field. Walls top out at #d8d8d8, the same ceiling as that
        pattern, so body text keeps 13.3:1 and muted text 3.0:1 if either lands
        on one.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="demo">
      <h2>Default</h2>
      <div class="panel">
        <MazeField />
      </div>
      <p class="caption">
        44px rooms, 55% of dead ends braided back open. Braiding leaves loops in
        the maze, so the ball usually has a way around rather than one forced
        route. The thread behind the ball is the route it actually took.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo">
      <h2>Tighter rooms, quicker ball</h2>
      <div class="panel">
        <MazeField cell={28} ballRadius={4} speed={7.5} glow={120} height="360px" />
      </div>
      <p class="caption">
        28px rooms read as texture rather than architecture, and the ball covers
        ground fast enough that the corridors feel like a route rather than a
        slog.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo">
      <h2>Perfect maze, no braiding</h2>
      <div class="panel">
        <MazeField cell={64} braid={0} speed={5} height="360px" />
      </div>
      <p class="caption">
        Every dead end left in place. Exactly one route between any two rooms,
        so the ball's path is forced: it doubles back out of blind corridors and
        the travel reads as longer and more deliberate.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo">
      <h2>With a way out</h2>
      <div class="panel">
        <MazeField cell={34} exit exitX={0.82} exitY={0.5} height="360px" />
      </div>
      <p class="caption">
        An exit gives the maze somewhere to get to. Walking the ball onto it
        dissolves the maze outward from that point and fires
        <code>mazefield:solved</code>, which bubbles and carries the exit's
        position, so the page can stand something real where the ring was. The
        404 page puts a door home there. Reload to carve a new one.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo">
      <h2>As a page background</h2>
      <div class="panel overlay-panel">
        <MazeField cell={48} class="overlay-maze" height="100%" />
        <div class="overlay-content">
          <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
          <h3>Let's work together.</h3>
          <p class="overlay-muted">
            This paragraph uses the muted text color, the hardest case to keep
            readable over the pattern. Run the ball underneath it to see the
            walls at their darkest behind live text.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="caption">
        The same component behind content. It is marked aria-hidden and ignores
        pointer events, so it never interferes with text or links. Set
        <code>fixed</code> to pin it to the viewport behind a whole page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .maze-page {
    max-width: var(--max-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-7) var(--page-padding) var(--space-8);
  }

  .page-head {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-7);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    font-weight: 300;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .intro {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
  }

  .note {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .demo {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-7);
  }

  .demo h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .panel {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-bg);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .caption {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .caption code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }

  .overlay-panel {
    position: relative;
    height: 380px;
  }

  .overlay-panel :global(.overlay-maze) {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .overlay-content {
    position: relative;
    height: 100%;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: var(--space-6);
    max-width: 520px;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .overlay-content h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    font-weight: 300;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .overlay-muted {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
